// CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// The prior strategy relied on the model to decide when to emit "<<" and thus
// often never entered constrained mode, which explains the failure to include
// << >> spans. The revised strategy actively biases generation toward opening a
// constrained span while outside one, using short unconstrained steps with a
// strong boost on "<<". Once inside a span, it generates only parser-valid
// tokens and closes immediately when the constrained prefix is complete, so the
// arithmetic content remains inside delimiters. EOS is treated as terminal in
// both modes. This change prioritizes actually producing constrained math spans
// rather than waiting passively for them to appear.
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
generated := generatedPrefix;
insideConstrainedOut := insideConstrained;
currentConstrainedOut := currentConstrained;
cost := 0;

